<h1>How To Make A Tuna Sandwich</h1>
<p>This is a quick and easy instruction guide on how to make a tuna sandwich. This can be eaten as a lunch item or a snack and can be combined with any toppings of your choice, such as cucumber, lettuce or raw chopped bell pepper. This recipe is a guide to making a basic sandwich.</p>
<img src="https://somethingaboutsandwiches.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/tuna-cucumber-sandwich.jpg" alt="An image of a tuna sandwich" width="400">
<h2>Ingredients</h2> 
<ul>
<li> Canned Tuna </li>
<li> Mayonnaise </li>
<li> 2 Slices of bread </li>
<li> Cucumber </li>
</ul>

<h2>Instructions</h2>
<ol> 
<li> Empty a can of tuna into a bowl. </li>
<li> Add Mayonnaise and stir well until you create a spread. </li>
<li> Cut 5 slices of cucumber.</li>
<li> Spread the tuna mix onto a slice of bread. </li>
<li> Add the layer of cucumber slices. </li>
<li> Close the sandwich with the other slice of bread. </li>
<li> Slice the sandwich in half and enjoy. </li>
</ol>
